<title>USA: MCI, British Telecom confirm.</title>
<headline>MCI, British Telecom confirm.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Concert, the new company to be formed by the proposed merger of MCI Communications Corp and British Telecom, will list its American Depositary Shares - the equivalent of common stock - on the New York Stock Exchange, MCI and British Telecom said Friday.</p>
<p>The ADSs will begin trading on the NYSE upon completion of the BT/MCI merger, the companies said.</p>
<p>Ordinary shares will trade on the London Stock Exchange, the companies said.</p>
<p>Shares also will be traded on the Tokyo Stock Exchange, the companies said.</p>
<p>Company executives have said they expect the merger to close in autumn.</p>
</text>
